{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":40000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"b655e574572c9e084639485ebf66678f2299b26f92da1fd29043a46eedddf8c0","packTokens":18201,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":236,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"drafts","tokens":17728,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":5,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"merge"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMerge three independent spec drafts into one spec (same format rules as the drafts).\nEvery merged requirement lists in \"alignment\" which draft requirements it came from, as \"d<draft>:<REQ-id>\" (e.g. \"d1:REQ-2\"). Keep a requirement even if only one draft has it. Never write a requirement that is in no draft.\nWhen drafts conflict, keep both readings as separate requirements and add a conflict entry. Renumber merged requirements REQ-1.. and their ACs AC-<req>.<n>.\nEach Then names what a test reads, using at least one of these words: response, status, returned, row, record, call, request, sent, email, message, error, event, field, value, count, list, file, screen, page, shown, displayed. \"Sign-in succeeds\" fails; \"The response status is 200\" passes. Reword a draft's Then that doesn't, without changing what it checks.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"drafts\" kind=\"spec-drafts\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"draft\": \"d1\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"ASM-1 and ASM-11: procurement and receiving data are supplied mock/source records; no live connector is required.\",\n   \"ASM-2 and ASM-12 through ASM-14: import errors are presented per row, unmatched records remain pending and unavailable to pen operations, over-capacity mappings are rejected, and repeated source identifiers are reported as duplicates.\",\n   \"ASM-3 and ASM-15: forecasts use current measured ADG when available, otherwise a configured default, and use editable per-lot target weight and gain-rate assumptions.\",\n   \"Q-2 and ASM-4: wastage ratio affects consumption estimates and projections; actual wastage is a separate movement when entered; inventory projections do not add low-stock alerts.\",\n   \"Q-4 and Q-5: feed conversion uses as-fed pounds and feed cost per pound of gain is not full ROI or profitability.\",\n   \"Q-6 and ASM-5: optimization compares cost and recorded nutrition values against user-specified targets or constraints; users select a suggestion before use.\",\n   \"Q-3, Q-7, and ASM-6: activities can be unplanned, link to an existing plan when available, and use separate quantities for each affected lot in a multi-lot pen.\",\n   \"ASM-7 and ASM-17: users can edit or delete feeding and weight events, and affected displayed series and metrics are refreshed from API responses.\",\n   \"Q-8: lot total gain is based on average-weight change and headcount applicable at the measurement dates.\",\n   \"ASM-8 and ASM-19: the report date range selects the latest weight reading in range and feeding events up to that reading; an on-screen filtered list and CSV export satisfy the export requirement.\",\n   \"ASM-9 and ASM-20: the separate demo dataset is loaded on demand, with added, already-present, and failed records reported separately and partial loads not labeled complete.\",\n   \"Q-1: all users have the same access to product areas and operational controls.\",\n   \"ASM-10: prompt history is omitted from the project and demo area.\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"At viewport widths of 320, 768, and 1440 CSS px, document horizontal overflow is 0 CSS px.\",\n    \"text\": \"Every page shall reflow for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths without horizontal page overflow.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n    \"metric\": \"At a 320 CSS px viewport width, every primary touch control has a hit area of at least 44 × 44 CSS px.\",\n    \"text\": \"Interactive controls on narrow phone layouts shall be touch-sized.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"Live procurement-system connector; the web app uses mock/source records only (ASM-1, ASM-11).\",\n   \"Yard-level aggregate dashboard stretch goal (I-8, ASM-21).\",\n   \"Prompt-history display (ASM-10).\",\n   \"API-SIDE: authoritative persistence, upstream connector implementation, duplicate-import and capacity enforcement, inventory ledger enforcement, and authoritative feed-to-gain calculations; this web specification tests user inputs, API responses, and what the responsive web app displays.\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The mock procurement and receiving API responses contain PO lines and receiving records\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays each record's source identifier, vendor, cost, headcount, weight, and row status\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens the import preview\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A PO line is mapped to multiple lots and the lots are mapped to pens\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays each PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen mapping with the returned pen capacity and current animal count\",\n      \"when\": \"the user reviews the mapping screen\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The import response includes duplicate, unmatched, or over-capacity rows\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays a row-level duplicate, pending-mapping, or capacity-limit status and does not present unmatched records as available for pen operations\",\n      \"when\": \"the user reviews import results or attempts an over-capacity assignment\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let users preview mock procurement and receiving records, import them, and map PO lines to one or more lots and lots to pens.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"ASM-1\",\n     \"ASM-2\",\n     \"ASM-11\",\n     \"ASM-12\",\n     \"ASM-13\",\n     \"ASM-14\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Incoming animal data and the forecast response are available for a lot\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned target weight, projected market date, and gain-rate basis\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens that lot's forecast\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A lot has editable target-weight and gain-rate assumptions\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the submitted assumption values and the forecast response associated with those values\",\n      \"when\": \"the user changes either assumption and requests a forecast\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The forecast response includes a feeding adjustment or sale-timing recommendation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned recommendation\",\n      \"when\": \"the user views the lot forecast\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let users view and configure lot target weights and gain-rate assumptions and view projected market dates and target weights from incoming animal data.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"ASM-3\",\n     \"ASM-15\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The inventory response contains feed items and stock movements\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays each item's name, category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry matter percentage, energy value, storage location, and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens inventory\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The user selects a wastage ratio and a projection horizon\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned projected balance with the selected ratio and the horizon labeled as daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, or annual\",\n      \"when\": \"the user requests an inventory projection\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user records actual wastage as a stock movement\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned wastage movement separately from consumption estimates and projections\",\n      \"when\": \"the movement is saved\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall provide inventory screens for ingredient details, stock movements, configurable wastage, and consumption projections across daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"ASM-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The user creates or opens a ration\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the ration name and type, ingredient names and proportions, dry matter percentage, energy value, calculated cost per pound, and intended animal type or weight range\",\n      \"when\": \"the ration screen is displayed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The user submits nutritional targets or constraints for ration optimization\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned feasible mixes with their ingredient proportions, recorded nutrition values, and costs in lowest-cost order\",\n      \"when\": \"feasible suggestions are returned\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A ration optimization suggestion is displayed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows no suggested ration as applied, and when the user selects one the screen displays that selected ration for use\",\n      \"when\": \"the user has not selected a suggestion\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let users create and compare rations using ingredient proportions, nutrition values, and costs, and require an explicit user selection before using an optimized ration suggestion.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-6\",\n     \"ASM-5\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A pen has an animal count and the user selects a date, ration, and daily bunk rate\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned plan with date, pen, assigned lot where applicable, animal count, ration, planned quantity, planned feeding time, quantity per animal, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and plan status\",\n      \"when\": \"the user generates a feeding plan\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A feeding plan exists for a pen and date\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the plan's returned status as Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens that plan\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let users generate and review dated feeding plans for specific pens using a daily bunk rate, selected ration, and pen animal count.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-5\",\n     \"ASM-6\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user records a feeding activity for a pen and date where a plan exists\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned plan link, planned and actual quantities, actual-minus-planned variance, feeding status, feed cost, energy value, and inventory consumed\",\n      \"when\": \"the activity is saved\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user records a feeding activity for a pen and date with no plan\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned activity as unplanned and does not require a plan link\",\n      \"when\": \"the activity is saved\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A pen contains multiple lots\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen requires a separate quantity for each affected lot and displays the returned lot-level quantities\",\n      \"when\": \"the user enters an activity's actual quantity\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API refuses an activity because available inventory is insufficient\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned shortage error and does not show the activity as saved\",\n      \"when\": \"the user submits the activity\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let users record feeding activities against a pen and date with an optional plan link and display returned activity costs, inventory consumption, and plan variance.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"I-5\",\n     \"Q-3\",\n     \"Q-7\",\n     \"ASM-6\",\n     \"ASM-18\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user records a weight measurement for a lot\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned measurement date, number of animals weighed, average animal weight, total lot weight, weight gain since the prior measurement, and notes\",\n      \"when\": \"the measurement is saved\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A lot has multiple saved weight measurements\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned readings in date order as a time series\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens its weight history\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user edits or deletes a saved weight measurement\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned series and recalculated metric values\",\n      \"when\": \"the API returns the updated measurement series and metrics\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let users record, view, edit, and delete lot weight measurements and display the lot's measurement time series.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-6\",\n     \"ASM-7\",\n     \"ASM-17\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A lot has a receiving date, feeding events, and weight readings\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays returned days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain per pound, and projected ship date\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens its performance metrics\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A lot's inventory units require conversion to pounds for feed-to-gain reporting\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays total feed consumed in as-fed pounds as the feed conversion ratio basis\",\n      \"when\": \"the user views performance metrics\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns total lot weight gain based on average-weight change and headcount applicable at the measurement dates\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned total gain and average daily gain values\",\n      \"when\": \"the user views lot performance\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A feeding or weight event is saved, edited, or deleted\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the latest returned feed-to-gain metric values\",\n      \"when\": \"the user returns to the affected lot's performance view\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A lot's feed cost per pound of gain is displayed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.5\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen labels the value as feed cost per pound of gain and does not label it ROI or profitability\",\n      \"when\": \"the user views the metric label\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall display lot feed-to-gain metrics returned after feeding and weight events, using the selected date range and the returned as-fed pound basis for feed conversion.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-7\",\n     \"Q-4\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"Q-8\",\n     \"ASM-3\",\n     \"ASM-7\",\n     \"ASM-8\",\n     \"ASM-17\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The dashboard API returns lot, pen, inventory, ration, plan, feeding, and performance data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays active lot and pen counts, animals per lot and pen, feed inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rate per pen, planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting and current weight, total weight gain, average daily gain, feed conversion ratio, feed cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens the dashboard\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The reports API returns pen and lot comparisons\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays returned rankings or values for pen feed consumption, lot feed conversion and average daily gain, ration usage, plan alignment, over- or underfeeding, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of weight gain\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens an operational report\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall provide lot- and pen-level dashboards and reports for operational and performance metrics.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-8\",\n     \"ASM-21\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The report response contains lot performance data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays ADG, FCR, and cost of gain for multiple lots with the date range, breed, sex, and pen filters\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens the feed-to-gain report\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The user selects a valid date range, breed, sex, or pen filter\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned filtered lot list and metric values\",\n      \"when\": \"the user applies the filters\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The report contains filtered lot results\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the browser downloads a CSV file containing the displayed report rows and metrics\",\n      \"when\": \"the user selects CSV export\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API refuses an invalid date range or unsupported filter value\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned error message\",\n      \"when\": \"the user applies the filter\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall provide a feed-to-gain report that compares lots and supports date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters with CSV export.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"ASM-8\",\n     \"ASM-19\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The sample dataset is available\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen identifies the dataset as a separate demo dataset and provides an on-demand load control\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens the sample-data screen\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A sample-data load returns added, already-present, or failed records\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays separate counts and record details for added, already-present, and failed data and does not label a partial load as complete\",\n      \"when\": \"the user views the load result\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let users load a clearly labeled, separate sample dataset on demand and show its load results.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-10\",\n     \"ASM-1\",\n     \"ASM-9\",\n     \"ASM-11\",\n     \"ASM-20\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user opens the project and demo area\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the page displays the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, an app demonstration, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis\",\n      \"when\": \"the page is rendered\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall provide a project and demo area with the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demonstration, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-11\",\n     \"ASM-10\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Two users open the web app\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"each screen displays the same product areas and operational controls to both users\",\n      \"when\": \"each views operational records, cost and performance views, import screens, and data-entry screens\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall expose the same product areas and operational controls to all users without role-dependent restrictions.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"Q-1\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"suggestions\": []\n },\n {\n  \"draft\": \"d2\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"The browser web app presents data and outcomes returned by the separate API service; acceptance criteria for this spec verify the web app's screens and interactions.\",\n   \"Procurement and receiving synchronization uses the supplied mock upstream records and does not require a live external connector (ASM-1, ASM-11).\",\n   \"CSV export satisfies the requested CSV-or-PDF export, and no custom report builder is included (ASM-19).\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"At viewport widths of 320, 768, and 1280 CSS pixels, 100% of in-scope pages render without page-level horizontal overflow; at 320 CSS pixels, every interactive target is at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels.\",\n    \"text\": \"Every in-scope page shall be responsive for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths and usable with touch on narrow screens.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"I-1 live procurement-system connector; use supplied mock/source data only (ASM-1, ASM-11).\",\n   \"I-3 low-stock or stockout alerts (ASM-4).\",\n   \"I-8 yard-level aggregate dashboard; treated as a stretch goal (ASM-21).\",\n   \"I-11 prompt history and overview of prompts used to build the solution (ASM-10).\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The mock source contains purchase-order and receiving records with vendor, source identifier, cost, head-count, and weight values.\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the imported field values and separate added, duplicate, and failed row counts.\",\n      \"when\": \"A user starts synchronization and opens its result.\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The mock source contains a row that cannot be imported.\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows that row and its reported failure reason.\",\n      \"when\": \"A user opens the synchronization result.\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let users synchronize the supplied mock purchase-order and receiving records and review vendor, source identifier, cost, head-count, and weight fields with added, duplicate, and failed row counts.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"ASM-1\",\n     \"ASM-11\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An imported purchase-order line is eligible for mapping and a fetched pen has available capacity.\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the purchase-order-to-lot-to-pen traceability and the assigned lot in the pen view.\",\n      \"when\": \"A user maps the line to multiple lots and assigns a lot to that pen.\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An imported record has no lot or pen mapping, or an assignment exceeds the fetched pen capacity.\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows unresolved records as pending and unavailable for pen operations, and shows the capacity refusal and limit for an over-capacity assignment.\",\n      \"when\": \"A user opens the mapping and pen views or attempts the assignment.\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A purchase-order or receiving record has already been imported using its upstream identifier.\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the duplicate outcome and does not show a second imported record for that identifier.\",\n      \"when\": \"A user synchronizes the same records again.\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When an imported purchase-order line or receipt needs mapping, the feedlot web app shall let users map a purchase-order line to one or more lots and lots to fetched pens, keep unresolved records visibly pending and unavailable to pen operations, and display capacity and duplicate-import outcomes.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"ASM-2\",\n     \"ASM-12\",\n     \"ASM-13\",\n     \"ASM-14\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A lot has a current measured ADG, a target weight, and incoming animal data.\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the configured target weight and the projected market date based on the measured ADG.\",\n      \"when\": \"A user opens the lot forecast.\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A lot has no current measured ADG and has a configured default gain rate and target weight.\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then