ms and stock movements, configure a wastage ratio for consumption estimates and projections, and review projected balances at daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"ASM-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user has entered ration name, type, ingredients, proportions, dry matter, energy, and intended animal type or weight range.\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the ration fields and its calculated cost per pound.\",\n      \"when\": \"The user saves and views the ration.\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Ingredients have recorded cost and nutrition values and a user has specified nutritional targets or constraints.\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows feasible mixes and their costs, and no suggestion is applied until the user selects it.\",\n      \"when\": \"The user requests an optimization comparison.\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let users create and maintain rations with ingredient proportions, nutrition values, intended animal ranges, and calculated cost, and compare feasible low-cost mixes for user-specified nutritional targets or constraints before a user selects a suggestion for use.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"Q-6\",\n     \"ASM-5\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A pen has an animal count and bunk rate and a user selects a ration and plan date.\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the pen, assigned lot information, plan date, ration, planned quantity, quantity per animal, feeding time, feed cost, expected energy, and plan status.\",\n      \"when\": \"